<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leicester</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leicester is a city in the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midlands">Midlands</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, on the River Soar. It began as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ratae-corieltauvorum">Ratae Corieltauvorum</a>, the Roman capital of the Corieltauvi, became an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> bishopric and one of the Five Boroughs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danelaw">Danelaw</a>, and grew into a county and market town. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-iii-of-england">Richard III</a> was buried there after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bosworth-field">Battle of Bosworth</a> in 1485, and his remains were rediscovered in 2012.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leicester.jpg" alt="Leicester" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NotFromUtrecht · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leicester_Clock_Tower_wide_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
